{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310560,"nonce":"LkTfLh2Nfwnfiy6+lWVeWBcq88A=","title":"RETRACTED — read this first","message":"The premise of this file is wrong. The mac-vs-Linux gap was an artifact of running\nthe corpus with a COPY of the binary in /tmp, which resolves haxe-std differently\n(exe-relative walk). With `RAYZOR=$PWD/target/release/rayzor` the mac scores 411 and\n**linux-only passes = 0** — every case listed below as 'Linux passes, mac fails'\npasses on the mac. See [[feedback_conformance_must_use_in_repo_binary]].\n\nWHAT SURVIVES: (1) tier-dependent cases are real — Issue2570 passes tiered, fails\nunder --llvm, deterministically, same binary same dir; (2) Issue4323 flipped between\ntwo full runs of the same binary, twice — the harness's one genuinely flaky case.\nEverything else below is the confound.\n\n---\n\n---\nname: bugs_conformance_bistable_mode_cluster\ndescription: \"RETRACTED 2026-09-03. The mac-vs-Linux gap was NOT REAL — it was my /tmp-binary-copy confound (see feedback_conformance_must_use_in_repo_binary). With the in-repo binary, linux-only passes = 0. Kept only for the two findings that survive.\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n- NUC 405 ⊇ CI 402 (exact); mac 382. ~33 linux-only passes / ~10 mac-only.\n- **Staged inputs BYTE-IDENTICAL** across platforms (md5 of every staged file; an\n  apparent set difference was MY diff's locale collation, not the harness).\n- **Harness parsing is CORRECT on both platforms**: 0 status-vs-log inconsistencies\n  across all 36 divergent cases on each side; runwith.py converts negative\n  returncodes to 128+signo; classification handles signal-number differences.\n  NUC logs carry ANSI color where mac logs do not — cosmetic only (status greps\n  anchor on test-emitted lines).\n- The phi-closure's \"+32/−9\" lists ≈ the linux/mac divergence sets — a SOURCE\n  change flipped the mac to the linux-side outcome set. Still unexplained.\n\n- \"Issue2570 flips with a byte-identical binary\" was largely MY INVOCATION VARIANCE:\n  2570 is TIER-DEPENDENT and deterministic — tiered default PASSES 8/8, --llvm FAILS\n  5/5 (E0803), same binary same dir. The harness default is LLVM=0 (tiered);\n  solo probes that added --llvm measured a different tier.\n- Snapshot ruled out twice over: payloads deterministic (2 timestamp bytes), AND\n  RAYZOR_IGNORE_EMBEDDED_SNAPSHOT=1 reproduces the same outcomes.\n- Sibling-load coupling: NOT reproducible (2570 solo-vs-load identical per tier).\n- Issue4323 single-flip stands as the one true same-binary harness flake observed.\n\n1. **Tier-dependent cases** (Issue2570-class): tiered vs --llvm disagree,\n   deterministically. E0803 fires only under --llvm there.\n2. **Platform-dependent cases** (Issue3528-class, \"Cannot find name 'Some'\"):\n   byte-identical inputs, fails mac / passes linux, BOTH tiers, snapshot ignored or\n   not. Leading hypothesis: platform-#if stdlib content differs → global\n   SymbolId/TypeId layout shifts → id-order-sensitive resolution (the E0803\n   candidate loop over field_index_map; bare-ctor resolution) picks differently.\n   Fix direction = order-independent resolution (the declaration-based-resolution\n   root fix), NOT chasing per-case flips.\n\n- Probes landed (env `RAYZOR_RESOLVE_TRACE=1`): E0200-unresolved dump at\n  expr/mod.rs (table-wide same-name scan) + E0803 candidate dump in\n  lookups.rs::resolve_field_index_candidates.\n- **THE PROBE BUILD ITSELF FLIPPED THE MODE**: Issue3528 fail→PASS and\n  Issue2570(tiered) pass→FAIL, coupled and anticorrelated — an INERT\n  env-gated eprintln reproduces the phi-closure flip. The mode is\n  f(compiled binary), full stop.\n- Snapshot exonerated THREE ways: payload-deterministic; IGNORE_EMBEDDED\n  reproduces outcomes; 3 snapshot-only regenerations (3 distinct binaries)\n  → outcomes stable.\n- NOT addresses: outcomes per-run stable under ASLR. NOT per-process hash\n  seeds (same reason). InternedString=u32. Hot read_dirs sorted.\n- CHICKEN-AND-EGG: observing mode A via instrumentation produces mode B.\n\nInstrument `Some` resolution + E0803 candidate sets (RAYZOR_STDLIB_ALIAS_LOG /\ntargeted eprintln behind an env) and diff mac-vs-NUC for ONE case each; that names\nthe exact table whose order diverges. Then make THAT resolution order-independent.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_conformance_bistable_mode_cluster` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}